#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0370 expect=noViolation domain=CO
#note "Authority: SDTM and SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0370 (Condition: IDVAR ^= null; Rule: IDVAR is a variable in the domain = RDOMAIN). The referenced DM carries its columns in lower case; the IDVAR cell names USUBJID as the standard spells it. The IDVAR cell is a string and stays exact; the referenced dataset's column list is a name list in the dataset's spelling, which the rule upper-cases (CIT 3) -> USUBJID is a variable of DM -> no violation. The boundary twin is CDISC-CG0370-invalid_lowercase_idvar_value-CO (a lowercase IDVAR cell still fires)."
dataset CO label="Comments"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RDOMAIN type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col IDVAR type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col COVAL type=Char label="Comment"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | CO | 01-701-1015 | DM | USUBJID | 01-701-1015 | Subject comment
---

dataset DM label=Demographics
col studyid type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col domain type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col usubjid type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015
---
